# dependencies and build output
node_modules/
vscode-extension/out/
*.vsix
# C2: `vscode-extension/core/mlview` is the analyzer the VSIX SHIPS, and it is a
# BUILT artifact, not a source of truth. `tools/sync-core.py` writes it, `npm run
# compile`, `npm run package` and `scripts/build.*` all run that first, and
# `tools/verify.py --vsix` checks the built copy against `analyzer/src/mlview`.
# One analyzer is tracked in this repository (`analyzer/src/mlview`) plus one
# vendored copy that a marketplace install of the Claude Code plugin needs
# verbatim (`claude-plugin/vendor/mlview`, which goes away once the wheel is on
# PyPI). A third tracked copy only ever added 96 files of review surface.
vscode-extension/core/
# PACKAGING: `python -m build --wheel analyzer` (scripts/build.sh step 6) writes both.
analyzer/dist/
analyzer/build/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# generated demo artifacts (scripts/e2e regenerates them)
.mlview/
webview/.mlview/
# MLV-P11: `python analyzer/tools/gen_gallery.py` renders ~90 self-contained reports
# (~30 MB) from the rule fixtures and the clean corpus. Zero new content, so it is
# generated on demand and never committed.
docs/gallery/

# `python tools/public_corpus.py fetch` clones 24 third-party repositories here
# (hundreds of MB). It is a local working directory, never repository content.
.public-corpus/

# local orchestration backups and scratch
# C5: `.workflows/` held the multi-agent orchestration scripts of past sprints —
# session artifacts full of absolute machine paths, not part of the product.
.workflows/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# local virtual environment (macOS setup)
.venv/
